1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,528
Your protocol note says two hundred fifty micrograms.

2
00:00:03,528 --> 00:00:05,664
Your vial talks in milligrams.

3
00:00:05,664 --> 00:00:10,546
Quick quiz: is that zero point two five milligrams, or two point five?

4
00:00:10,546 --> 00:00:13,684
One milligram is one thousand micrograms.

5
00:00:13,684 --> 00:00:18,437
So two hundred fifty micrograms is zero point two five milligrams.

6
00:00:18,437 --> 00:00:21,627
Pick two point five, and you're off by ten times.

7
00:00:21,627 --> 00:00:27,278
Watch it on a real vial: ten milligrams with five milliliters gives two per milliliter.

8
00:00:27,278 --> 00:00:31,992
Two hundred fifty micrograms is zero point one two five milliliters.

9
00:00:31,992 --> 00:00:33,736
Twelve point five units.

10
00:00:33,736 --> 00:00:37,200
BuddyPept converts mcg and mg for you.

11
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,453
Free, at Buddy Pept dot com.

12
